Hi

it seems correct.  but always, simulate data from the true model and
then use inla to estimate it back. if you have done it right (and with
many observations) you'll get your model estimated back.  (use
family="gaussian" and simulate gaussian observations, as then there is
no approximation errors, just numerical integration errors).

Best
H

