Hi,
I am attampting to jointly model two point pattern using the spde approach and get the following error message,

GMRFLib version 3.0-0-snapshot, has recived error no [12]
	Reason    : The Newton-Raphson optimizer did not converge
	Message   : Condition `lambda < 1.0 / lambda_lim' is not TRUE
	Function  : GMRFLib_init_GMRF_approximation_store__intern
	File      : approx-inference.c
	Line      : 2694
	RCSId     : file: approx-inference.c  hgid: 15fa1e788b12  date: Fri Sep 20 09:14:11 2013 +0200

I initially built the model with 12 different pp's, but to illustrate I just used two code below,

t.1<-inla.stack(data=list(y=cbind(pp.1,NA),e=e.1),
                A=list(A.1,1),tag="pp1",
                effects=list(i=1:nv,bpp.1=rep(1,nv+nums[1])))
t.2<-inla.stack(data=list(y=cbind(NA,pp.2),e=e.2),
                A=list(A.2,1),tag="pp2",
                effects=list(j=1:nv,bpp.2=rep(1,nv+nums[2])))
t.ent<-inla.stack(t.1,t.2)
ft<-y ~ 0 + bpp.1 + bpp.2 + f(i,model=spde) + f(j,copy="i",fixed=FALSE)
t.st <http://t.st><-inla(ft,family=rep('poisson',2),
                data=inla.stack.data(t.ent),
                control.predictor=list(A=inla.stack.A(t.ent)),
                E=inla.stack.data(t.ent)$e,
           verbose=TRUE)

I ran the call again with verbose=T the output rather lengthy is below, from what I can see there is a problem with the optimiser trying to find post marginal for theta (i.e. evaluates to NAN), how do I therefore get the optimizer to converge (i.e. do I scale, or set priors?);
Many Thanks in advance
Charlotte

